trademarks of Proton AG. These builds receive no QA from Proton and come
with no warranty of any kind.

What is added on top of upstream
--------------------------------
  packaging/arch/PKGBUILD        Arch package, built from upstream source
  packaging/arch/lumo-desktop.desktop
                                 Desktop entry (name marked "unofficial",
                                 StartupWMClass=lumo-desktop, proton-lumo://
                                 scheme handler)
  packaging/appimage/            Tauri config override for the AppImage build
  .github/workflows/             AppImage build, Arch repo publishing,
                                 upstream release watcher

Third-party components
----------------------
On Linux the app uses the host's WebKitGTK, GTK 3 and libayatana-appindicator
rather than bundling a browser engine, so their licences and notices are
provided by the distribution packages. Bundled Rust and JavaScript
dependencies keep their own licences; see Cargo.toml, package.json and the
upstream repository for the full dependency set.

